<VI _name="lvbd_tidy_constants.vi" description="Tidies every block diagram constant of one VI the way a LabVIEW developer would place it, then saves the VI in place: the label is hidden (its text stays, so tools that find a constant by label still do), a string constant made only of white space switches to '\5C' Codes Display, and an array constant shows as many elements as it holds (one at least, twenty at most). Each constant is cast to each class on its own error chain, so a cast that does not apply skips that step and nothing else. No object reference is closed inside the loop: the casts are the traversal's own refnums, and closing one made every later cast Error 1055 (measured 2026-11-11); closing the VI reference releases them. The main error chain runs THROUGH the loop in a shift register: without that data dependency Save.Instrument and the VI reference's close ran beside the loop, and the object references died under it - every cast Error 1055, on some runs from the first constant (measured 2026-11-11). User-forum feedback of 2026-11-11.">
